    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00003",
      "class": "mechanism-figure scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00219:caption:fig-00003-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00219:alt:fig-00003-alt",
          "text": "Reaction mechanism for ketone or aldehyde to imine through five steps: nucleophilic attack of amine, proton transfer generating neutral carbinolamine, protonation of hydroxy, iminium ion formation, and deprotonation to imine."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_19_08_005.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00005",
      "segmentId": "m00219:para:para-00005"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00004",
      "class": "unnumbered",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00219:alt:fig-00004-alt",
          "text": "First reaction shows the formation of cyclohexanone oxime between cyclohexanone and hydroxylamine. Second reaction shows the formation of acetone-2,4-dinitrophenylhydrazone from acetone and 2,4-dinitrophenylhydrazine. Water is the by-product in both reactions."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_19_08_004.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00006",
      "segmentId": "m00219:para:para-00006"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00005",
      "class": "mechanism-figure scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00219:caption:fig-00005-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00219:alt:fig-00005-alt",
          "text": "Reaction mechanism shows enamine formation from ketone or aldehyde by reacting with secondary amine through four steps: nucleophilic addition causing carbinolamine formation, protonation, formation of iminium ion, deprotonation to enamine."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_19_08_003.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
